      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Column Layout\nA column layout stores all values of one\ncolumn together. A Python dictionary shows the\nidea. Each key is a column, and each value is\nthe list of that column's values. [pyarrow](ht\ntps://arrow.apache.org/docs/python/generated/p\nyarrow.Table.html#pyarrow.Table.to_pydict) is\nthe Python library for Apache Arrow. Its\n`to_pydict()` method returns the example table\nas `{'id': [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], 'city':\n['Perth', 'Perth', 'Sydney', 'Sydney',\n'Perth', 'Perth'], 'fare': [12.5, 8.0, 20.0,\n15.5, 9.0, 11.0]}`. A Parquet file adds one\ndetail. It cuts each list into pieces, one for\neach row group.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-47455e3cb314",
      "originalText": "Column Layout\nA column layout stores all values of one column together. A Python dictionary shows the idea. Each key is a column, and each value is the list of that column's values. [pyarrow](https://arrow.apache.org/docs/python/generated/pyarrow.Table.html#pyarrow.Table.to_pydict) is the Python library for Apache Arrow. Its `to_pydict()` method returns the example table as `{'id': [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], 'city': ['Perth', 'Perth', 'Sydney', 'Sydney', 'Perth', 'Perth'], 'fare': [12.5, 8.0, 20.0, 15.5, 9.0, 11.0]}`. A Parquet file adds one detail. It cuts each list into pieces, one for each row group.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "column-layout"
      }
    },
