      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Many Files Form One Table\nA large table is usually many Parquet files.\nEach file has its own footer, which describes\nonly that file. A table format such as Apache\nIceberg records which files form the table. A\nSnowflake Iceberg table is an example. Its\nrows sit in many Parquet files in cloud\nstorage, and the Iceberg metadata names the\nfiles. The [Iceberg\nmap](../iceberg/iceberg.md) explains the table\nformat, and the [Iceberg in Snowflake map](../\nsnowflake/iceberg/snowflake-iceberg.md) covers\nSnowflake's side.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-f643f8e37a19",
      "originalText": "Many Files Form One Table\nA large table is usually many Parquet files. Each file has its own footer, which describes only that file. A table format such as Apache Iceberg records which files form the table. A Snowflake Iceberg table is an example. Its rows sit in many Parquet files in cloud storage, and the Iceberg metadata names the files. The [Iceberg map](../iceberg/iceberg.md) explains the table format, and the [Iceberg in Snowflake map](../snowflake/iceberg/snowflake-iceberg.md) covers Snowflake's side.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "many-files-form-one-table"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3799428674,
      "isDeleted": false,
