    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4880880429,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-d7eb6b340a11",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1312.0,
      "y": 1907.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 420.0,
      "seed": 221241,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Footer\nThe footer is the last part of the file. After\nit come its length (4 bytes) and the closing\n`PAR1` (4 bytes). In the example file, the\nfooter covers bytes 606 to 1,587. The footer\nholds three things:\n\n- The schema, which lists the column names and\ntypes ([file metadata](https://github.com/apac\nhe/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/src/main/thrift\n/parquet.thrift#L1422-L1445)).\n- The byte range, codec, and encodings of\nevery column chunk ([column metadata](https://\ngithub.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/\nsrc/main/thrift/parquet.thrift#L922-L959)).\n- The minimum and maximum value of every\ncolumn chunk.\n\nA reader starts here. It reads the end of the\nfile, finds the footer length, and then reads\nthe footer. The writer puts the footer last,\nso that it can write the file in one pass ([sp\necification](https://github.com/apache/parquet\n-format/blob/ec90dd4/README.md#L109-L121)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d7eb6b340a11",
      "originalText": "Footer\nThe footer is the last part of the file. After it come its length (4 bytes) and the closing `PAR1` (4 bytes). In the example file, the footer covers bytes 606 to 1,587. The footer holds three things:\n\n- The schema, which lists the column names and types ([file metadata](https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/src/main/thrift/parquet.thrift#L1422-L1445)).\n- The byte range, codec, and encodings of every column chunk ([column metadata](https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/src/main/thrift/parquet.thrift#L922-L959)).\n- The minimum and maximum value of every column chunk.\n\nA reader starts here. It reads the end of the file, finds the footer length, and then reads the footer. The writer puts the footer last, so that it can write the file in one pass ([specification](https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/README.md#L109-L121)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "footer"
      }
    },
