      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2809965615,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-d43ee08881f9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1891.6000000000001,
      "y": 1907.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 525.0,
      "seed": 82358,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Three Queries on One Table\nThe times are the median of 5 runs on one\nthread, with the files in the operating system\ncache. They show CPU work and no disk delay.\nThe byte counts are exact.\n\n- Sum of `fare` where `city` is `Perth`. This\nneeds 2 of the 4 columns. Parquet reads\n705,192 bytes and takes 4.5 ms. SQLite takes\n12 ms. CSV reads 19,625,110 bytes and takes 23\nms.\n- Sum of `fare` where `id` is at least 200000.\nThis needs 2 columns from 1 of the 3 row\ngroups. Parquet reads 866,416 bytes and takes\n0.6 ms. SQLite takes 2.7 ms. CSV reads\n19,625,110 bytes and takes 21 ms.\n- Read every column of every row. Parquet\nreads 15,416,992 bytes and takes 9.8 ms. CSV\nreads 19,625,110 bytes and takes 25 ms.\n\nIn the first query, Parquet reads 28 times\nfewer bytes than CSV. Two steps make the gap.\nThe CSV text of `city` and `fare` alone takes\n4,736,208 bytes, which is 4.1 times fewer than\nthe whole file. Parquet stores those two\ncolumns in 639,656 bytes, and the footer read\nadds 65,536 bytes. Column Pruning, Encoding\nand Compression, and Row Group Skipping\nexplain the steps. In the third query, Parquet\nis still 2.6 times faster.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d43ee08881f9",
      "originalText": "Three Queries on One Table\nThe times are the median of 5 runs on one thread, with the files in the operating system cache. They show CPU work and no disk delay. The byte counts are exact.\n\n- Sum of `fare` where `city` is `Perth`. This needs 2 of the 4 columns. Parquet reads 705,192 bytes and takes 4.5 ms. SQLite takes 12 ms. CSV reads 19,625,110 bytes and takes 23 ms.\n- Sum of `fare` where `id` is at least 200000. This needs 2 columns from 1 of the 3 row groups. Parquet reads 866,416 bytes and takes 0.6 ms. SQLite takes 2.7 ms. CSV reads 19,625,110 bytes and takes 21 ms.\n- Read every column of every row. Parquet reads 15,416,992 bytes and takes 9.8 ms. CSV reads 19,625,110 bytes and takes 25 ms.\n\nIn the first query, Parquet reads 28 times fewer bytes than CSV. Two steps make the gap. The CSV text of `city` and `fare` alone takes 4,736,208 bytes, which is 4.1 times fewer than the whole file. Parquet stores those two columns in 639,656 bytes, and the footer read adds 65,536 bytes. Column Pruning, Encoding and Compression, and Row Group Skipping explain the steps. In the third query, Parquet is still 2.6 times faster.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "three-queries"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8736945468,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d11c13b0cd12",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1879.6000000000001,
      "y": 2167.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
