    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5521900683,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-d11c13b0cd12",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1891.6000000000001,
      "y": 2167.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 402.5,
      "seed": 852757,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Savings Grow With Table Width\nThe gain depends on how many columns a query\nskips. Each table here has 100,000 rows of\nrandom decimal numbers, and each query sums\nthe first column. Parquet reads the same\n334,234 bytes for every table, because the\nother columns are skipped.\n\n- 4 columns: the CSV file has 2,312,335 bytes,\nwhich is 6.9 times more than Parquet reads.\nParquet takes 0.2 ms and CSV takes 4.2 ms.\n- 20 columns: the CSV file has 11,561,921\nbytes, which is 35 times more. Parquet takes\n0.3 ms and CSV takes 17 ms.\n- 100 columns: the CSV file has 57,805,429\nbytes, which is 173 times more. Parquet takes\n0.4 ms and CSV takes 85 ms.\n\nA wide table with a narrow query gains the\nmost. Snowflake tables also store columns\nseparately, so a Snowflake query scans only\nthe columns that it references (see Column\nPruning).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-d11c13b0cd12",
      "originalText": "Savings Grow With Table Width\nThe gain depends on how many columns a query skips. Each table here has 100,000 rows of random decimal numbers, and each query sums the first column. Parquet reads the same 334,234 bytes for every table, because the other columns are skipped.\n\n- 4 columns: the CSV file has 2,312,335 bytes, which is 6.9 times more than Parquet reads. Parquet takes 0.2 ms and CSV takes 4.2 ms.\n- 20 columns: the CSV file has 11,561,921 bytes, which is 35 times more. Parquet takes 0.3 ms and CSV takes 17 ms.\n- 100 columns: the CSV file has 57,805,429 bytes, which is 173 times more. Parquet takes 0.4 ms and CSV takes 85 ms.\n\nA wide table with a narrow query gains the most. Snowflake tables also store columns separately, so a Snowflake query scans only the columns that it references (see Column Pruning).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "savings-grow-with-width"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2045721836,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-360d77bbb974",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1879.6000000000001,
      "y": 2297.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
      "seed": 519743,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
