      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2515729727,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-360d77bbb974",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1891.6000000000001,
      "y": 2297.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 735.0,
      "seed": 542958,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Savings Depend on Column Values\nParquet is efficient with compression for\nthree reasons. The writer encodes each column\nby its type before the codec runs. The writer\npicks the encoding and the codec for each\ncolumn, and the footer records both. A reader\ndecompresses only the pages of the columns\nthat a query needs.\n\nThe sizes below are rough. They come from the\ntest table with ZSTD as the codec. Each one\ncompares a Parquet column with the CSV text of\nthe same column, compressed with ZSTD too:\n\n- Four different city names: about 4 times\nsmaller. Dictionary encoding does this.\n- Ids that rise by one: thousands of times\nsmaller. Delta encoding stores only the step\nbetween neighbours, which is always 1.\n- Decimal fares: about 1.3 times smaller.\n- Random letters: about the same size. Only\nthe codec can shrink them, by about a third\nwith ZSTD and a few percent with SNAPPY.\n\nWith ZSTD, the whole table is about half its\nCSV size, in Parquet and in CSV alike. Parquet\nis only a few percent smaller than the\ncompressed CSV, because two thirds of the\ntable is random letters. A query on one column\ndecompresses about 20 times fewer bytes than a\ncompressed CSV file needs, and it runs about\n30 times faster.\n\nSnowflake compresses each column of a\nmicro-partition on its own and picks the\nalgorithm itself ([micro-partitions](https://d\nocs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-cluster\ning-micropartitions)). Iceberg writes Parquet\nfiles with ZSTD unless the table property\n`write.parquet.compression-codec` says\notherwise ([configuration](https://iceberg.apa\nche.org/docs/latest/configuration/)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-360d77bbb974",
      "originalText": "Savings Depend on Column Values\nParquet is efficient with compression for three reasons. The writer encodes each column by its type before the codec runs. The writer picks the encoding and the codec for each column, and the footer records both. A reader decompresses only the pages of the columns that a query needs.\n\nThe sizes below are rough. They come from the test table with ZSTD as the codec. Each one compares a Parquet column with the CSV text of the same column, compressed with ZSTD too:\n\n- Four different city names: about 4 times smaller. Dictionary encoding does this.\n- Ids that rise by one: thousands of times smaller. Delta encoding stores only the step between neighbours, which is always 1.\n- Decimal fares: about 1.3 times smaller.\n- Random letters: about the same size. Only the codec can shrink them, by about a third with ZSTD and a few percent with SNAPPY.\n\nWith ZSTD, the whole table is about half its CSV size, in Parquet and in CSV alike. Parquet is only a few percent smaller than the compressed CSV, because two thirds of the table is random letters. A query on one column decompresses about 20 times fewer bytes than a compressed CSV file needs, and it runs about 30 times faster.\n\nSnowflake compresses each column of a micro-partition on its own and picks the algorithm itself ([micro-partitions](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-clustering-micropartitions)). Iceberg writes Parquet files with ZSTD unless the table property `write.parquet.compression-codec` says otherwise ([configuration](https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/configuration/)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "savings-depend-on-values"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 6163176381,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-d45498bb6340",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1289.2,
      "y": 2167.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220.0,
      "seed": 209161,
      "groupIds": [],
