    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 7199315755,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-42f263f6eb8d",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1301.2,
      "y": 2583.125,
      "strokeColor": "#7C2D12",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 386.40000000000003,
      "height": 192.5,
      "seed": 419241,
      "groupIds": [
        "rhdjcntn"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Encoding and Compression\nThe writer prepares each page in two steps. It\nfirst encodes the values into a compact form,\nby using the type and the pattern of the\ncolumn. It then compresses the encoded bytes\nwith a codec, which is a compression method\nthat works on any bytes. A codec replaces a\nrepeated run of bytes with a short reference\nto its first copy, and it can give common\nbytes shorter bit codes. The first step works\nwell because a chunk holds one kind of value.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-42f263f6eb8d",
      "originalText": "Encoding and Compression\nThe writer prepares each page in two steps. It first encodes the values into a compact form, by using the type and the pattern of the column. It then compresses the encoded bytes with a codec, which is a compression method that works on any bytes. A codec replaces a repeated run of bytes with a short reference to its first copy, and it can give common bytes shorter bit codes. The first step works well because a chunk holds one kind of value.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
