    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8040947729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-6a28a06f2c9f",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1074.4,
      "y": 3649.75,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 386.40000000000003,
      "height": 910.0,
      "seed": 657001,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Files Are Written Once\nA writer creates a Parquet file in one pass,\nand engines then leave it unchanged. To change\ndata, an engine writes a new file. This is a\nhabit of engines, and the layout makes it\npractical. The format has no lock, and an\noverwrite is possible.\n\nThe footer comes last, so a writer needs one\npass over the data ([specification](https://gi\nthub.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/RE\nADME.md#L109-L121)). The footer records the\nbyte range and the minimum and maximum value\nof every chunk. These numbers describe the\nexact bytes before the footer.\n\nExperiments with pyarrow 18.1.0 in November\n2026, on copies of the example file, show what\nan overwrite does:\n\n- Replace one value with another value of the\nsame size, in a copy written with plain\nencoding and no compression. The file opens\nand returns the new value, 99.0 in place of\n20.0. The footer still says that the maximum\nof `fare` is 20.0. The filter `fare > 50`\nreturns 0 rows when it uses the footer, and 1\nrow after a full read. Two readers give two\nanswers.\n- Flip one byte inside a compressed chunk of\n109 bytes. Of the 109 possible flips, 60 break\nthe read, 15 return different values without\nan error, and 34 change nothing that a reader\nsees.\n- Insert one byte before a chunk. Every later\nbyte range in the footer is off by one, and\nthe read fails.\n- Flip one byte in the footer. Of the 981\npossible flips, 721 break the read.\n- Add page checksums. A writer can store a\nCRC32 checksum for each page ([specification](\nhttps://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/\nec90dd4/README.md#L224-L228)). With\n`write_page_checksum=True` when writing and\n`page_checksum_verification=True` when\nreading, pyarrow reports the same-size edit as\nan error: CRC checksum verification failed.\n\nA table format such as Apache Iceberg tracks\nwhich files are current. The [Iceberg\nmap](../iceberg/iceberg.md) describes its data\nfiles as immutable.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-6a28a06f2c9f",
      "originalText": "Files Are Written Once\nA writer creates a Parquet file in one pass, and engines then leave it unchanged. To change data, an engine writes a new file. This is a habit of engines, and the layout makes it practical. The format has no lock, and an overwrite is possible.\n\nThe footer comes last, so a writer needs one pass over the data ([specification](https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/README.md#L109-L121)). The footer records the byte range and the minimum and maximum value of every chunk. These numbers describe the exact bytes before the footer.\n\nExperiments with pyarrow 18.1.0 in November 2026, on copies of the example file, show what an overwrite does:\n\n- Replace one value with another value of the same size, in a copy written with plain encoding and no compression. The file opens and returns the new value, 99.0 in place of 20.0. The footer still says that the maximum of `fare` is 20.0. The filter `fare > 50` returns 0 rows when it uses the footer, and 1 row after a full read. Two readers give two answers.\n- Flip one byte inside a compressed chunk of 109 bytes. Of the 109 possible flips, 60 break the read, 15 return different values without an error, and 34 change nothing that a reader sees.\n- Insert one byte before a chunk. Every later byte range in the footer is off by one, and the read fails.\n- Flip one byte in the footer. Of the 981 possible flips, 721 break the read.\n- Add page checksums. A writer can store a CRC32 checksum for each page ([specification](https://github.com/apache/parquet-format/blob/ec90dd4/README.md#L224-L228)). With `write_page_checksum=True` when writing and `page_checksum_verification=True` when reading, pyarrow reports the same-size edit as an error: CRC checksum verification failed.\n\nA table format such as Apache Iceberg tracks which files are current. The [Iceberg map](../iceberg/iceberg.md) describes its data files as immutable.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "files-are-written-once"
      }
    },
